Make the following AOT compatibility fixes in /tmp/sv-f63e54eca000485bab49995792c2d4b0/before/. These files have IL2026/IL3050/IL2087/IL2090 warnings that need to be fixed.

## 1. ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs
The method `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` at line 30 calls `RegisterClientFactory` which has `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]`. Add these attributes to the method:

```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
[RequiresDynamicCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values requires generating dynamic code at runtime, for example instantiating generic types. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator (EnableConfigurationBindingGenerator=true) instead.")]
```

Add `using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;` to the file's usings.

## 2. ArmEnvironment.cs
Line 80: `public override string ToString() => JsonSerializer.Serialize(this);`

Replace with manual JSON construction that doesn't use JsonSerializer:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    return $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\",\"DefaultScope\":\"{DefaultScope}\"}}";
}
```

This avoids JsonSerializer entirely. Keep the existing usings.

## 3. ArmClientOptions.cs
Line 52: `var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);`

Replace with JsonDocument parsing:
```csharp
using var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
var allProfile = doc.RootElement;
var armProfile = allProfile.GetProperty("resource-manager");
foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile.EnumerateObject())
{
    var namespaceName = keyValuePair.Name;
    var element = keyValuePair.Value;

    foreach (var apiVersionProperty in element.EnumerateObject())
